  will come much much later after years of  teaching and healing after trial and  execution on an Easter morning but we're  back at the beginning and Phillip goes  to his friend with this mystery we have  found the one Moses spoke of he is Jesus  from Nazareth and Nathaniel rather  snarkily responds can anything good come  out of Nazareth imagine your best friend  coming to you and saying we have found  the leader the one who will save us and  he is Stanley from hoboken  that's what Jesus from Nazareth sounded  like to Nathaniel and so he laughs and  he snarkily says nothing good can come  from there but Philip is the needed  middleman he doesn't argue with  Nathaniel he doesn't get offended at his  snarky tone he just says okay come and  see Philip doesn't get theological or  political he doesn't try to entice  Nathaniel he says the words that  skeptical Nathaniel needs to hear trust  your own eyes come and see the Midwife  the middleman the messenger sees what  God is doing sees the need for God in  others and makes the connection the word  may come late at night to a boy a new  disciple needs just the right response  to call him forth to a life of purpose  the middleman is the one of whom Roman  says how beautiful are the feet of the  messenger that brings the good news  there's a wonderful story i read this  week by Reverend Cynthia Weems of First  United Methodist Church in Miami and  I'll quote from it because it's too good  not to hear her words she tells the  story of a middleman coming to her she's  in her first job as a minister in a big  Midwestern city she's in a urban church  since having tough times and she's just  started but she gets a request from a  friend to translate into Spanish for the  father of Victor an eleven-year-old boy  coming before the Youth Court because  he'd shot another child in the leg with  a BB gun at 11 year old she goes to  court she translates and Victor was  sentenced to 25 days community service  and Reverend Williams realized his  family lived just three blocks away from  her church and so she offered to let him  serve his community service there so he  came the next morning and he was given  the task of cleaning a dirty disused  youth room on the third floor and it was  told if he did it well he and his  friends could use it as a gathering  place so he worked hard  he took it seriously got the room in  order but his other community service  task was to help with Vacation Bible  School and Victor didn't like anything  with the word school in the title but he  came and he helped and he brought his  friends Fernando and Javier and Pedro  revin dreams rights that she didn't  really want to help Victor and his  family she didn't want to supervise  Victor for his project there were so  many other calls on her life she was a  new pastor visiting church families  denominational work all the tasks and  urban pastor has maintaining a building  in a changing neighborhood but during  the week of vacation bible school  Victor's friend Pedro came up to her at  one point and asked pastor you know  those community service hours that  Victor has how can I get some of those  she writes I was stunned to attention  all the other voices crying out for my  attention stopped and I was silent and I  listened the voice of the Lord was about  to speak it was clear and it came with a  challenge do kids have to shoot someone  with the BB gun before they're invited  to our church eleven-year-old Pedro  didn't know he was the messenger of god  but he was allowing the message to come  through loud and clear often the Bible  seems to be calling us to be superheroes  to be healers to be peacemakers to be  miracle workers but today's stories of  eli and Phillip and Pedro offer a  different kind of discipleship the  discipleship of making connections in my  preaching class last semester Tom kroger  and Nora Tisdale ask those second-year  prospective preachers to write a short  exercise for the end of the class just  